Status: DONE (technical evidence; human acceptance pending)
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/BowserBoyAdvance/issues/2
Milestone: First playable static GBA prototype
Dependencies: None
Purpose: Select a legally held local .gba ROM and actually play in the browser.

Tasks:
- [x] Verify a pinned emulator release and single-threaded GBA core.
- [x] Build responsive, accessible local-file selection and player shell.
- [x] Isolate the emulator lifecycle, inputs and explicit loading failures.
- [x] Verify actual frames and input with an original test cartridge.

Acceptance criteria:
- Local files never go to an application backend.
- GBA gameplay, keyboard input and mobile layout have runtime evidence.
- Wrong/oversized files produce actionable errors without destroying play.

Completion evidence:
- 2026-11-04: Real mGBA framebuffer changes with keyboard input; original
  Pixel Lab ROM, live CDN core, desktop Edge. Mobile touch controls accept taps.
- Browser UI verifies narrow layout, help dismissal and invalid file handling.
- See tests/browser/player.spec.mjs and docs/VERIFICATION.md for boundaries.

Completion log:
- 2026-11-03: Empty repository inspected; EmulatorJS 4.2.3 loader verified.
- 2026-11-04: Playable static prototype completed. No commercial ROM matrix or
  physical phone/controller acceptance implied.
